203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 162 0 R
/E (Speed control of DC motors is a fundamental problem in robotics, automation, and embedded systems. A motor operating in open loop cannot guarantee that the desired speed will be maintained, since variations in load, voltage, and friction affect its behavior. For this reason, closed-loop control strategies are commonly used to regulate motor speed accurately.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 162 0 R
/E (In this final challenge, the objective is to design and implement a closed-loop speed control system for a DC motor. The system must regulate the motor speed according to a reference signal generated from ROS, while estimating the actual motor velocity through encoder feedback. To achieve this, the solution integrates hardware and software components, including an ESP32 microcontroller, an L298N motor driver, a DC motor with encoder, and ROS nodes for command input and monitoring.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
