<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (The communication between the ESP32 and ROS2 is implemented using micro-ROS over a serial connection. The ESP32 works as a ROS node called motor_control, which receives the speed reference from the topic set_point and publishes the measured motor speed to the topic motor_output.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (On the ROS side, a separate node generates reference signals such as step, sine, square, or triangle waves and continuously publishes them to set_point. The ESP32 processes this reference, executes the PID controller, drives the motor through PWM, and sends the resulting speed back to ROS for monitoring.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
